{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For before those days</b> — before it was built, the hired laborer could not find what to do." "<b>And the word איננה</b> — refers to wages, for many words are found in both masculine and feminine forms. And R. Moses said: איננה refers back to the beast — there are no wages for the beast, for it is not from the adversary, the foe." "<b>And I sent</b> — to make strife."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "The phrase כי איננה מן הצר הצורר is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. 'R. Moses' likely refers to R. Moses Ibn Ezra or R. Moses HaKohen, resolved by inference."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:21.331789925Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}